From 9a3522bd35197fb90162e683aa6f96eaa159775f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Illya Antonyuk <illantalex84@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 18:01:04 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 76/77] media: si470x-i2c: power the receiver down after probe

Probe leaves the chip powered up and tuned, which costs about 17 mA of
the Sony Ericsson P1i's standby current. Stop it at the end of probe as
release does; open resets and starts it again. The supply stays on: after
a power cycle the chip chooses another bus mode and holds the I2C bus.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/media/radio/si470x/radio-si470x-i2c.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/radio/si470x/radio-si470x-i2c.c b/drivers/media/radio/si470x/radio-si470x-i2c.c
index 8173f0263..5141be901 100644
--- a/drivers/media/radio/si470x/radio-si470x-i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/media/radio/si470x/radio-si470x-i2c.c
@@ -479,6 +479,13 @@ static int si470x_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		goto err_all;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * Powerdown until the radio is opened (open resets and starts it): powered up
+	 * the chip draws about 17 mA (Sony Ericsson P1i standby). Its supply stays on:
+	 * after a power cycle it chooses another bus mode and holds the I2C bus.
+	 */
+	si470x_stop(radio);
+
 	/* register video device */
 	retval = video_register_device(&radio->videodev, VFL_TYPE_RADIO,
 			radio_nr);
-- 
